{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794058119,"nonce":"plhXnmAEGfOhONq1xzrT+tt4n70=","message":"Findings, 2026-11-07, against the deployed site (55f02eb2 docs deploy), reproduced on desktop Chrome.\n\n1. WebGL2 mesh panic (the Android 3D failure). With the worker forced onto the WebGL2 backend, mesh_3d_demo ends in a wasm unreachable: \"Mesh Bind Group Layout, binding 14 entry is invalid, Downlevel flags VERTEX_STORAGE are required but not supported\". Bindings 14 and 15 are the morph-target storage buffers; they were declared unconditionally, while mesh_dt.wgsl has no morph code. Fix in the working tree: the WebGL2 layout and bind group stop at binding 13. Verified that pipeline creation no longer panics under forced WebGL2 (local wasm swapped into the deployed page). Not yet verified: a rendered frame, because the local build could not preload the model's textures.\n\n2. Missing textures on iPhone (strangler skin, buster_drone). Reproduced by hiding texture-compression-bc from the worker's adapter on desktop WebGPU: gltf_animation_demo renders white and strangler_demo logs \"BC texture received but device has no TEXTURE_COMPRESSION_BC - binding default\". The glTF loader BC-encodes textures without knowing the device, and the mesh upload bound the 1x1 default when BC is unavailable. DamagedHelmet uses jpg and is unaffected. Fix in the working tree: new blinc_gpu::bc_decode expands BC1/3/4/5 to RGBA8 on the CPU and the mesh upload takes the uncompressed path (sRGB for colour slots). Decoder unit tests (hand-built blocks plus an encoder round trip) and the full blinc_gpu lib tests pass. Rendered result not yet seen; check the deployed demos with BC hidden after the next deploy. Android GPUs without BC (the Pixel) hit the same path.\n\n3. Not explained: Android Chrome showing the loading state for every demo. 2D demos load fine under forced WebGL2 on desktop, so this is not the WebGL2 backend alone. Needs a device session (adb reverse plus CDP) to see which phase stalls; no device was attached.","files":null}]}